          <text id="consent_screen-consent_script-label">
            <value>**Read this out loud to the household.**

Good morning. My name is (say your own name) and I am working with Dimagi on a survey to understand the circumstances of households in this area.

I would like to ask you some short questions about your household — who lives here, what the household has eaten in the last week, and some things the household may own. I will also take a photograph of the outside of your dwelling. It takes about ten minutes.

Taking part is your choice. You may say no, and nothing will happen to you if you do.

If you agree, you can still stop at any point, and you can skip any question you do not want to answer.

Your answers are confidential. I will not show them to your neighbours or to any other household. Your name is stored only so that this household can be told apart from others, and it is not attached to any published report about the results.

Your answers do not stay with me. They go to Dimagi and to the organisation running the graduation programme, and they will use them to decide which areas and which households the programme works with. A small sample of visits is also reviewed by a supervisor, who may see this household's answers.

One thing I must be clear about: taking part does not mean you will be selected for the programme. That decision is made later, by other people, and most households I speak to will not be enrolled. I cannot promise you anything today, and if you say no you lose nothing you would otherwise have had.

Do you agree to take part?</value>
            <value form="markdown">**Read this out loud to the household.**

Good morning. My name is (say your own name) and I am working with Dimagi on a survey to understand the circumstances of households in this area.

I would like to ask you some short questions about your household — who lives here, what the household has eaten in the last week, and some things the household may own. I will also take a photograph of the outside of your dwelling. It takes about ten minutes.

Taking part is your choice. You may say no, and nothing will happen to you if you do.

If you agree, you can still stop at any point, and you can skip any question you do not want to answer.

Your answers are confidential. I will not show them to your neighbours or to any other household. Your name is stored only so that this household can be told apart from others, and it is not attached to any published report about the results.

Your answers do not stay with me. They go to Dimagi and to the organisation running the graduation programme, and they will use them to decide which areas and which households the programme works with. A small sample of visits is also reviewed by a supervisor, who may see this household's answers.

One thing I must be clear about: taking part does not mean you will be selected for the programme. That decision is made later, by other people, and most households I speak to will not be enrolled. I cannot promise you anything today, and if you say no you lose nothing you would otherwise have had.

Do you agree to take part?</value>
          </text>
