          <text id="roster_intro-label">
            <value>**List every member of this household, one person per row.**

Add one row for each person. Do not ask the household how many people live here — you decide that yourself, by applying the definition below to each person you are told about.

A household is a group of people who usually sleep in the same dwelling and take their meals together, and who either have been part of the household for at least 6 of the 12 months preceding the interview, or are currently members. It can equally consist of persons temporarily absent but returning soon, such as students.</value>
